      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from a 13th‑century church dedicated to Saint Nicholas, which gave the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sint-Niklaas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The market square, the largest in Belgium, was laid out by Margaret II and still hosts the country’s biggest Christmas tree.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sint-Niklaas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Gerardus Mercator Museum in Sint‑Niklaas traces the history of cartography back to its origins.",
